course: dictionary
lesson: 2478
title: Daydream
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A daydream is a set of pleasant thoughts you have while you are awake. Your mind drifts away from what is around you. «Daydreaming is a normal part of thinking, as long as you are not missing something important, like a road to cross.» So daydreaming is fine most of the time, but not when it stops you noticing danger.
explain: Daydream can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, it is the thought itself: «lost in a daydream». As a verb, to daydream means to think about pleasant things when you should be doing something else, so a teacher might say, «Stop daydreaming and listen!»
explain: Use the clues around the word. Is the pupil staring out of the window and smiling? Has someone just asked a question that was missed? The words around the word tell you whether daydreaming is a harmless escape or a problem. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: «I was daydreaming» should still make sense.
explain: A daydream can also mean a wish or plan that is not likely to come true. A girl might have a daydream of flying a plane one day. She does not expect it to happen soon, but she enjoys thinking about it.
fact: Daydream can be a noun (a daydream) or a verb (to daydream).
fact: «Daydream» means pleasant thoughts you have while awake that take your mind away from what is around you.
fact: «Daydreaming» means thinking about pleasant things instead of what you should be doing.
fact: Daydreaming is normal, but it is a problem when you miss something important, like a road to cross.
fact: A daydream can also be a wish or plan that is not likely to come true.
exercise: «She was lost in a daydream by the window.» What does lost in a daydream mean? | Looking for something she dropped | Asleep in bed | *Thinking pleasant thoughts, away from what is around her | Lost her way home
exercise: A teacher says, «Stop daydreaming and listen!» What should the pupil do? | Close the book and go to sleep | Dream of listening to music | *Stop thinking about other things and pay attention | Go outside to play
exercise: «Daydreaming is a normal part of thinking, as long as you are not missing something important.» According to this, when is daydreaming a problem? | *When you miss something important, like a road to cross | When you think happy thoughts | When you are in bed at night | When you are drawing a picture
test: In «Her daydream was to become a famous singer», what kind of word is daydream? | Adverb | Adjective | *Noun | Verb
test: «His daydream is to own a racing bike.» What does daydream mean here? | A bad dream at night | A plan the teacher made | A wide awake dream at school | *A wish that is not likely to come true
exam: In «Sam likes to daydream about being a footballer», what does daydream about mean? | *To think happy thoughts about something you would like | To kick a ball at the goal | To run fast around the football pitch | To sleep and forget the game
